sbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>DOI, TSUTOMU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIBAURA MECHATRONICS CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIN-ETSU HANDOTAI CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ABE TATSUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>DOI TSUTOMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ABE, TATSUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>DOI, TSUTOMU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method is provided for cleaning a semiconductor wafer by removing laser marks on it. Laser marks (51) are detected directly or indirectly in noncontact manner while a semiconductor wafer (10) is rotated. The rotation of the semiconductor wafer is controlled in response to detected laser marks, and liquid with ultrasonic vibrations is sprayed.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention se rapporte à un procédé de nettoyage d'une plaquette de semi-conducteur qui consiste à supprimer des marques de laser sur ladite plaquette. Les marques de laser (51) sont détectées directement ou indirectement et sans contact pendant que la plaquette de semi-conducteur (10) est en rotation. On commande la rotation de la plaquette de semi-conducteur en fonction de la détection des marques de laser, puis on utilise des vibrations ultrasonores pour pulvériser un liquide.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that t